import ../../../testing/driver.dl

appearance source appearance:
    height is 100

document example:
    read only editor "Library" containing "Aé🙂B\nC" using source appearance
    link "Next" to "" using no UI appearance

set instance to an instance of example
set window to the address of instance
set node to the control labeled "Library" in window
set view to a UI view of window sized 400 by 240 using font "regular" with the test UI driver
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 3 key 258 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition ((view's text focus = node) and (view's input context's active = false)) reporting "A read-only editor lost keyboard focus or activated platform editing."
queue UI input of kind 3 key 268 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 2 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 3 key 262 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 1 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 3 key 262 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 1 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 3 key 67 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 2 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
set surface to view's window as a pointer to test UI surface
require condition ((surface's copied = "Aé") and (view's selection's caret = 3)) reporting "Read-only text could not be navigated, selected and copied on Unicode boundaries."
queue UI input of kind 4 key 0 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "typed" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 3 key 259 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 3 key 261 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 3 key 257 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 3 key 88 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 2 containing "" in (the address of view)
queue UI input of kind 13 key 1 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "platform edit" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
set value to the UI value for node in window
require condition ((value's text = "Aé🙂B\nC") and (value's undo = @intrinsic("construct", a pointer to UI text edit))) reporting "Read-only input or platform events changed the source or its history."
set UI control node read only false in window
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (view's input context's active) reporting "Unlocking text did not restore platform editing."
queue UI input of kind 4 key 0 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "Z" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (value's text = "Z🙂B\nC") reporting "Unlocking a source discarded its original selection."
set epoch to view's input context's epoch
receive UI composition (the string form of "tentative") for epoch at phase 1 selecting 9 through 9 in (the address of view)
set UI control node read only true in window
queue UI input of kind 13 key epoch at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "late IME commit" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (((view's input context's active = false) and (view's selection's composing = false)) and (value's text = "Z🙂B\nC")) reporting "Locking a source kept tentative composition or accepted a late platform commit."
set the text of "Library" in window to "Updated"
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition ((value's text = "Updated") and (view's input context's active = false)) reporting "A programmatic update was blocked or re-enabled read-only text input."
queue UI input of kind 3 key 258 at 0.0 0.0 with modifiers 0 containing "" in (the address of view)
ignore update UI view (the address of view)
require condition (view's focused's node's text = "Next") reporting "Tab could not leave a read-only editor."
close the address of view
close window

window field example:
    read only text field "Token" containing "public"
set instance to an instance of field example
set node to the control labeled "Token" in (the address of instance)
require condition ((the UI value for node in (the address of instance))'s read only) reporting "A text field lost its declarative read-only policy."
close the address of instance
print line "Read-only text keeps selection, copy, navigation and programmatic updates while excluding edits and IME."
